cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sharpecheck, please cite it as below."
title: sharpecheck
abstract: >-
  Sharpe-ratio inference in Python (iid, Mertens/Opdyke, AR(1)-adjusted, HAC,
  studentized block bootstrap, exact noncentral t, PSR, MinTRL, DSR, Ledoit-Wolf
  difference tests, Romano-Wolf stepdown), with a Monte Carlo check of interval
  coverage and test size.
type: software
authors:
  - name: sharpecheck contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/h-a-forster/sharpecheck"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0.dev0
keywords:
  - sharpe ratio
  - hypothesis testing
  - bootstrap
  - multiple testing
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Ledoit
        given-names: Olivier
      - family-names: Wolf
        given-names: Michael
    title: Robust performance hypothesis testing with the Sharpe ratio
    journal: Journal of Empirical Finance
    year: 2008
    doi: 10.1016/j.jempfin.2008.03.002
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Lo
        given-names: Andrew W.
    title: The statistics of Sharpe ratios
    journal: Financial Analysts Journal
    year: 2002
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Bailey
        given-names: David H.
      - family-names: López de Prado
        given-names: Marcos
    title: "The deflated Sharpe ratio: correcting for selection bias, backtest overfitting and non-normality"
    journal: Journal of Portfolio Management
    year: 2014
